(:adr
  :id "D1"
  :shortcode "D1"
  :title "Git-Native Intent Ledger and Grounded ADR Engine"
  :status :active
  :date "2026-09-07"
  :cluster "memory-architecture"
  :deciders ["steps-implementer" "steps-plan-reviewer"]
  :problem "Autonomous software agents require deterministic, persistent access to architectural decisions, operational invariants, and normative constraints. Traditional approaches embed annotations (@REQ, @ADR) directly into source code comments or store records in external cloud databases. Both approaches introduce severe failure modes: comment annotations decay and pollute token context, while cloud datab..."
  :drivers ["Zero-Comment Invariant: 0 inline comments or @REQ tags in code packages." "Git-Native Parity: Architectural decisions and constraints must branch and merge atomically with code." "Progressive Disclosure: Sub-200 token query footprints via compact AST representation." "AST Implicit Traceability: Binds decisions directly to symbol paths (module/function)."]
  :decision "Adopt Git-Native Intent Ledger (.asl/mem/intent.asn) paired with narrative ADR records in .asl/mem/decisions/. All traceability binds through .asl/mem/trace.asn using canonical symbol paths."
  :invariants ["c1" "c3"]
  :consequences [(:pos "Deterministic execution and verified boundary constraints") (:neg "Requires adhering to strict verification gates")])
